    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The first state to leave the Central American federation, in 1838, long torn between liberal León and conservative <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>.</li><li>Its possible canal route drew British, filibuster and American interventions, from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-walker">William Walker</a> in 1856 to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states-marine-corps">US Marines</a> in 1912–1933.</li><li>The Somoza dynasty ruled from 1936 to 1979 until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sandinista-national-liberation-front">Sandinista</a> revolution; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daniel-ortega">Daniel Ortega</a> has governed again since 2007.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>In 1902 opponents of a Nicaraguan canal sent US senators Nicaraguan postage stamps showing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/momotombo">Momotombo</a> volcano in eruption; shortly afterwards the Senate chose Panama.</p></aside>
    </section>

